& [IdentityAccountingMcpDurableStoreP2] is a bounded filesystem custody adapter and local stdio MCP transport for a P1 AccountingJournal
  + [SnapshotStore] persists each complete canonical journal generation as a create-new content-addressed file and recovers one unique maximal replay-consistent lineage
  + [IdentityAccountingMcpServer] serializes concurrent requests through one mutex persists a successful mutation before publishing it in memory and returns typed structured content
  + [Tool] exposes the exact P1 AccountingHostRequest union without adding semantic operations

  = IAP-01 must: operate only in one explicit existing non-symlink directory and inspect only regular files named as lowercase SHA-256 JSON snapshots
  = IAP-02 must: bound scanned entry count individual snapshot bytes request bytes and emitted snapshot bytes before allocation or mutation
  = IAP-03 must: decode every admitted snapshot through P1 canonical validation and require filename digest journal digest requested journal identity and basket continuity to agree
  = IAP-04 must: recover one unique maximal journal whose retained history contains every earlier admitted snapshot as an exact prefix and reject forks or incomparable maxima
  = IAP-05 must: persist successors with create-new write-all and file sync before advancing process-local state
  = IAP-06 must: treat an existing content-addressed target as idempotent only when its exact bytes equal the candidate and otherwise refuse collision
  = IAP-07 must: leave in-memory journal unchanged when encoding creation writing syncing or validation fails
  = IAP-08 must: expose one closed-world MCP tool carrying an exact AccountingHostRequest and complete typed response or bounded fault
  = IAP-09 must: preserve P1 stale journal ledger and object compare-and-set behavior under concurrent calls so one equal-root mutation succeeds and the other refuses
  = IAP-10 must: perform no filesystem write for project resolve inspect read-ledger read-event or inspect-journal operations
  = IAP-11 must: restart from persisted snapshots with the same exact journal head and make all prior ledgers and events readable
  = IAP-12 must: deny unknown fields oversized arguments malformed store state response encoding ambiguity and unsupported tool names without partial semantic success
  = IAP-13 must: provide a stdio-only executable requiring explicit store directory journal identity and byte bounds
  = IAP-14 must: invoke no model open no network listener infer no hidden state sign no meaning and authorize no external effect beyond declared snapshot custody

& [Delineation]
  + [inside] is local snapshot directory scan canonical recovery create-new durable snapshot write process mutex exact P1 execution stdio MCP and typed faults
  + [boundary] is the operator provisions and protects the directory chooses retention backup and access policy and supplies an initial canonical snapshot
  + [outside] is network service authentication encryption distributed consensus garbage collection semantic truth provider inference effect authorization and cross-host replication

& [SatisfactionSignature]
